{"name":"Vapour Trail","hex":"#f5eedf","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vapour trail","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A contrail."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vapour_trail"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vapour Trail (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Vapour Trail\" is a song by British shoegaze band Ride. It is the closing track of the band's debut album, Nowhere (1990), released on Creation Records, and was later released as a single in the United States in early 1991. Written by lead guitarist Andy Bell, the song features a distinctive swirling guitar riff, a strong, fill-based drum beat, and a coda that includes a string quartet."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/0e/Ride_-_Vapour_Trail.jpg/330px-Ride_-_Vapour_Trail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vapour_Trail_(song)","wikidata":"Q7915345"},{"title":"Contrail","blocks":[{"text":"Contrails or vapour trails are line-shaped clouds produced by aircraft engine exhaust or changes in air pressure, typically at aircraft cruising altitudes several kilometres/miles above the Earth's surface. They are composed primarily of water, in the form of ice crystals. The combination of water vapor in aircraft engine exhaust and the low ambient temperatures at high altitudes cause the trails' formation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Jet-contrails-tokyosky-japan-2018.webm/330px--Jet-contrails-tokyosky-japan-2018.webm.jpg","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Contrail","wikidata":"Q207546"},{"title":"Vapor","blocks":[{"text":"In physics, a vapor or vapour is a substance in the gas phase at a temperature lower than its critical temperature, which means that the vapor can be condensed to a liquid by increasing the pressure on it without reducing the temperature of the vapor. A vapor is different from an aerosol. An aerosol is a suspension of tiny particles of liquid, solid, or both within a gas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Nitrogen_dioxide_gas.jpg/330px-Nitrogen_dioxide_gas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vapor","wikidata":"Q255722"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/0e/Ride_-_Vapour_Trail.jpg/330px-Ride_-_Vapour_Trail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/0e/Ride_-_Vapour_Trail.jpg/330px-Ride_-_Vapour_Trail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARide_-_Vapour_Trail.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Qantas_Boeing_747-400_VH-OJU_over_Starbeyevo_Kustov.jpg/500px-Qantas_Boeing_747-400_VH-OJU_over_Starbeyevo_Kustov.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Qantas_Boeing_747-400_VH-OJU_over_Starbeyevo_Kustov.jpg/1280px-Qantas_Boeing_747-400_VH-OJU_over_Starbeyevo_Kustov.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Qantas_Boeing_747-400_VH-OJU_over_Starbeyevo_Kustov.jpg/500px-Qantas_Boeing_747-400_VH-OJU_over_Starbeyevo_Kustov.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Contrails of a Boeing 747-438 from Qantas at 11,000 m (36,000 ft)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AQantas_Boeing_747-400_VH-OJU_over_Starbeyevo_Kustov.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Propeller_tip_vortices_being_generated_by_P-40N1_Warhawk_VH-ZOC_at_Temora.jpg/500px-Propeller_tip_vortices_being_generated_by_P-40N1_Warhawk_VH-ZOC_at_Temora.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conten