ud_chamber.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Vapor_being_used_in_a_cloud_chamber.jpg/1280px-Vapor_being_used_in_a_cloud_chamber.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Vapor_being_used_in_a_cloud_chamber.jpg/500px-Vapor_being_used_in_a_cloud_chamber.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"If the vapor pressure exceeds the equilibrium value, it becomes supersaturated and condenses on any available nucleation sites e. g. particles of dust. This principle is used in cloud chambers, where particles of radiation are visualized because they nucleate formation of water droplets.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVapor_being_used_in_a_cloud_chamber.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Crepuscular_Rays_Beam_through_the_Mist_Blown_from_Takkakaw_Falls.jpg/500px-Crepuscular_Rays_Beam_through_the_Mist_Blown_from_Takkakaw_Falls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Crepuscular_Rays_Beam_through_the_Mist_Blown_from_Takkakaw_Falls.jpg/1280px-Crepuscular_Rays_Beam_through_the_Mist_Blown_from_Takkakaw_Falls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Crepuscular_Rays_Beam_through_the_Mist_Blown_from_Takkakaw_Falls.jpg/500px-Crepuscular_Rays_Beam_through_the_Mist_Blown_from_Takkakaw_Falls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Invisible water vapor condenses to form visible water droplets called mist","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACrepuscular_Rays_Beam_through_the_Mist_Blown_from_Takkakaw_Falls.jpg"}],"sounds":{}}}